WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.867
Self-attention.

2
00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:06.800
The mechanism that replaced recurrence, and powers every modern language model.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.363
Self-attention turns attention inward.

4
00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:12.167
The sequence looks at itself.

5
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.790
Every token computes weights over every other token,

6
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:20.200
itself included, and rebuilds its representation as a weighted blend.

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.595
Take this sentence.

8
00:00:22.595 --> 00:00:24.167
The word it is ambiguous.

9
00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.698
It sends a query, and every word answers with a key.

10
00:00:27.698 --> 00:00:29.500
Each match gives a raw score.

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.252
Softmax turns the scores into weights.

12
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:33.800
Tank gets sixty percent.

13
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.328
So the new vector for it is mostly built from tank.

14
00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:40.367
Every other token does the same, simultaneously.

15
00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:42.700
Why did this win?

16
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.233
Compare it with an RNN.

17
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:49.400
An RNN passes information along step by step, and it degrades on the way.

18
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:53.067
Self-attention connects every pair of tokens directly.

19
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:57.900
And it is just matrix multiplication, exactly what GPUs love.

20
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.533
The catch is that cost grows as n squared with sequence length.

21
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:04.367
Here's the whole thing in NumPy.

22
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:07.500
Six tokens, each a sixty four number embedding.

23
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:12.900
Multiplying X by its own transpose scores every token against every token.

24
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.900
Softmax turns scores into weights, and one more multiply blends the tokens.

25
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.133
Same shape in, same shape out.

26
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:23.367
Now the price of all-to-all attention.

27
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.521
An eight thousand token mission log needs sixty

28
00:01:26.521 --> 00:01:29.800
four million pairwise scores in every attention layer.

29
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.933
Double it to sixteen thousand, and the bill is four times, not two.

30
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.533
This shapes real design.

31
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:39.200
Embedding a long log whole is expensive.

32
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.067
That's why a RAG system chunks its documents.

33
00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:45.840
And why just increasing the context window is never free

34
00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.500
when your GPU latency budget is three hundred milliseconds.

35
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.530
Let's recap.

36
00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:54.433
Each token blends all tokens, in parallel.

37
00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:56.633
Direct links replaced recurrence.

38
00:01:56.933 --> 00:01:58.933
It's just matrix multiplication.

39
00:01:59.233 --> 00:02:01.656
But cost grows as n squared.

40
00:02:01.656 --> 00:02:02.867
Next up: NLTK.
